				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/maliceaforethought" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2902864); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2902864&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606984845" alt="MaliceAforethought" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2902864)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/maliceaforethought" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2902864); return false;" >MaliceAforethought</a></span> <span class="odate time_1569062559 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">21 Sep 2019 10:42</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4370727">
									

<p>I have two main issues with this.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The first is that I've always been iffy about the use of 'Pataphysics as a synonym for Metafiction, since that wasn't its original intended meaning within the SCP-verse. Rimple, The Great Hippo, and a few other authors have constructed specific narratives regarding the true fictional/metafictional nature of 'pataphysics, which I feel this sort of thing &#8212; despite being an <em>excellent</em> metafictional anomaly in its own right &#8212; dilutes slightly. But in the interest of breaking out the high-energy Therisno Cannons, I'm not gonna let that minor gripe stand in the way of an upvote.</p>
<p>The second is something I've been wavering about, and is why I originally no-voted: because this is 'pataphysical/metafictional/metaphysical/'patafictional/whatever, the antagonist here is the author of the original SCP-166, or at least their fictional analogue. This isn't a defence of the original by any means; it's just that this blurs the line between in-universe fiction and out-of-universe fiction in a way that makes me a little bit uncomfortable. But, then again, I suppose that's the point.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Regardless, those things aren't enough to stop me from thoroughly enjoying it. It's certainly better than the original :P</p>

							</div>

								
					
